<title>SWEDEN: Sweden must join EMU if meets criteria - Lamfalussy.</title>
<headline>Sweden must join EMU if meets criteria - Lamfalussy.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The head of the European Monetary Institute Alexandre Lamfalussy said on Monday Sweden must join the European Union's monetary union (EMU) if it fulfills the Maastricht convergence criteria.  </p>
<p>&quot;As I understand the situation, I believe that Sweden is obliged to join the EMU if the criteria are fulfilled. But negotiations about this are underway,&quot; Lamfalussy told reporters after an EMU seminar on Monday.</p>
<p>The Swedish interpretation that the decision about joining the EMU should be a political one made by the Swedish parliament has not been accepted by other EU governments, Lamfalussy said.</p>
<p>&quot;This is in many ways a grey zone that nobody really knows how to interpret,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom, +46-8-700 1006</p>
